@283[7]. The reformation of the Church. Treated of.

@294. To "create" = to reform. Explained, Illustrated. @295.

@--[3]. The reformation of the gentiles. Treated of.

@356[3]. For man is reformed by the dissipation of evils and falsities by truths applied to life.

@419[14]. Reformation as to the natural man. Treated of.

@633[8]. The instauration anew, or reformation, of the Church. Signified.

@721[12]. The instauration of the Church, and the reformation of those who are of the Church. Signified. @730[27].

@803[2]. 8. Thus, and no otherwise, is man reformed.

@837[4]. Reformation is effected in this order...

@946[end]. As man cannot be reformed, unless he thinks, etc. from himself...

@971[2]. This Reciprocal is necessary for reformation.

@1093[end]. He is reformed by the admission of his thoughts into the Societies of Heaven.

@1150[4]. For externals must be reformed through internals...

@1155[3]. Man is not reformed by external means, but by internal means... Still, he is further reformed by external means, when ho has previously been reformed by internal means. Explained.

@1158[2]. Hence everyone can be reformed; and to be reformed is nothing else than to be removed from evil loves.

@--[3]. Such do those become who have once been reformed, and do not remain so.

@1170[6]. Thus it is the will which is to be reformed... @1171[5].

@DWis 4. The analogy between the formation of man... and his reformation. Explained.

@Char 210[2]. Those who do good from obedience are those who are reformed. @LJPost 352.

Reformed, The.; Reformati.
Reformation, The.; Reformatio.
Reformer.; Reformator.
See <Protestant>.

@LJ 47. The Last Judgment was executed... lastly upon the Reformed.

@48. In the middle appeared those called the Reformed, distinct according to their countries. Enumerated. @LJCont 20.

