@--[3]. The remission (or forgiveness) of sins (is supposed to be) the wiping of them away... and that after the remission they go clean... but the case is quite different with the remission of sins. The Lord remits sins to everyone... but they are not on that account remitted, unless the man performs serious repentance, and desists from evils, and then lives a life of faith and charity, and this up to the end of his life. When he does this, he receives new spiritual life from the Lord, and when from this life he regards the evils of his former life, and feels aversion and horror for them, then, first, are the evils remitted; for the man is then kept in truths and goods by the Lord, and is withheld from evils. Hence it is evident what is the remission of sins, and that this cannot exist within an hour, or within a year. This is known by the Church, for it is said to those who approach the Holy Supper that their sins are remitted if they begin a new life...

