@216[end]. The consorts are revived by the hope of its continuation after death.

@294[4]. The man is revived by the influent meretricious sphere.

@TCR 434. Assemblies of friendship... for the revival of the sensuous things of the body.

@569[2]. Stenches revive their nostrils and hearts.

@SE 4700[end]. He inquired where he could be revived, and at last he was revived.

@5941. This is their quiet, and revival.

@AE 1214[2]. Minds are revived, recreated, and excited... by the odours and flavours of plants.

Revive.; Revivere.

@AC 5972. "The spirit of Jacob... revived" (Genesis 45:27) = new life in natural good.

@AR 153. When they die and revive as to the spirit, which is usually on the third day...

@CL 532[2]. The Angels said, This is for the sake of the end that the Christian Church, which is founded upon the Word, and is now at its end, may revive again, and draw breath through Heaven from the Lord.

@AE 418[3]. "The breath" from which they "revived" (Ezekiel 37:10) = spiritual life, which is life according to the truths of the Word. @666[3].

@SConf 39. 11. The Word, through which the Church would revive. Signified.

